-- title:
--   The q+1 branch primes of a Drinfeld chart ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, discretely valued, adically complete for its maximal ideal) whose maximal ideal is generated by an element $\pi$ and contains $q$; let $c \in \mathfrak m_W$ be nonzero. Let $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u$ and $v$ units and with $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1)$, the difference of $f$ and `drinfeldForm`, lying in $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$. Put $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(c)\,v - f\,u)$ and write $\mathrm{mk}_S$ for the quotient map. Call a prime $P \subset S$ a branch prime if $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\pi)) \in P$ and at least one of $\mathrm{mk}_S(X_0)$, $\mathrm{mk}_S(X_1)$ lies outside $P$, and say that $P$ has direction $(a,b) \in \mathbb Z^2$ if $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(a)X_0 + C(b)X_1 + h) \in P$ for some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$. The theorem asserts four things: every pair $(a,b)$ of integers not both divisible by $q$ is the direction of some branch prime; every branch prime has a direction $(a,b)$ with $(a,b)$ not both divisible by $q$; two branch primes with such directions $(a_1,b_1)$ and $(a_2,b_2)$ coincide if and only if $q \mid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$; and for every branch prime $P$ and every $s \in P$ there exist $r \notin P$ and $s' \in S$ with $rs = \mathrm{mk}_S(C(\pi))\,s'$, i.e. $P$ becomes generated by $\pi$ after localisation at $P$.
--
--   This is the local statement that the special fibre of a Drinfeld-type chart at a supersingular point has exactly $q+1$ smooth branches, indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ through the tangent cone $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$, with each branch prime of multiplicity one; it holds for an arbitrary nonzero chart constant $c$ in the maximal ideal. It is used in the analysis of the integral two-chart model of the modular curve at full level, where the branch primes and their directions are compared under the maps induced by the chart witnesses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart_branchPrimes_of_sub_drinfeldForm_mem_pow.lean

